9--> IAM Users
     --> Represents an individual person(developer, tester).
	 --> Can have username + password (console access).
	 --> Can have access keys (CLI/SDK access).
	 
10--> IAM Groups
      --> A Collection of users with shared permissions.
	  --> Example:
	        Group: Developers, Policy: PowerUserAccess.
			Group: Viewers, Policy: ReadOnlyAcess.
		
11--> IAM Roles
      --> Temporary identities assumed by users, apps, or AWS services.
	  --> No permanent credentials (keys are short-lived).
	  --> Best practise for EC2, Lambda, EKS, CI/CD.
	  --> jaise EC2 instance ko jarurat padi AWS account of your access karne ki kuch jarurat ki wajah se toh temporary role hai IAM role
	      jo grant karke EC2 instance tumhare AWS account ko access kar sakta
	  
12--> IAM Policies
      --> JSON documents defining permissions.
	  
